# Docker's .dockerignore matching is NOT .gitignore matching: each pattern is
# matched against the whole path relative to the build context root
# (tools/blog-mcp -- see .github/workflows/blog-mcp-image.yml's `context:`),
# using Go's filepath.Match plus `**`. A bare `dist` therefore matches only
# the context root's own dist/ and does NOT match ui/dist the way a .gitignore
# entry would -- confirmed directly: before this file added the `**/` prefixes
# below, both ui/node_modules (108 MB) and ui/dist were silently uploaded into
# every build context, and so was tools/blog-mcp/.env (real local
# credentials). Every pattern below that must apply at any depth is spelled
# with an explicit `**/` prefix for exactly that reason.
#
# Keep in parity with Dockerfile's COPY instructions and with
# build/WorkflowChangeAreas.psm1's blog_mcp_image pattern list.
# build/Test-BlogMcpImageContract.ps1 fails CI if the three drift apart.
#
# Exception (`!`) rules are deliberately absent: the parity test's matcher
# implements simple last-match-wins, which is exact only while there are none.
# Adding one requires extending that matcher first.

# Dependencies -- reinstalled inside the image by `npm ci` in the build,
# ui-build, and deps stages. The bare `node_modules` this file used to carry
# left ui/node_modules in the context, where `COPY ui/ ./` then overwrote the
# ui-build stage's own freshly installed, correctly-platformed tree.
**/node_modules

# Build output -- regenerated inside the image; the runtime stage copies
# dist/ and ui/dist from the build stages, never from the context.
**/dist
**/dist-ssr
**/.vite
**/coverage
**/.cache

# Tests and fixtures -- blog_mcp_test inputs, never image inputs.
test

# Local environment and secrets. `.env` is a real, git-ignored credential file
# on developer machines; without this it is uploaded into every build context
# and retained in BuildKit's context cache. `.env.*` covers .env.example and
# the CI Compose fixture .env.ci as well.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Runtime/deployment configuration and the watcher's input directory --
# blog_mcp_compose concerns, not image inputs.
docker-compose.yml
watch

# Documentation and planning documents. Safe as a blanket rule: there are no
# .md files anywhere under src/, ui/src/, or ui/public/.
**/*.md

# Tooling config not used by any build script. ui/package.json's build is
# `tsc -b && vite build`; oxlint runs only via the separate `lint` script.
**/.oxlintrc.json

# VCS, container, editor, and OS metadata.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
**/.dockerignore
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.vscode
**/.idea
